      "body": "Kennewick is where High Point lives, so this is the town we know best. Roofs here take a specific beating. The high-desert sun bakes shingles from Southridge and Canyon Lakes to the older streets near downtown and the newer builds climbing above Zintel Canyon, and it does the quiet damage first. Day-to-night temperature swings crack aging asphalt, the wind off the Columbia lifts anything that was not fastened right, and the occasional hard winter freeze finds every tired flashing. A roof built for a mild, wet climate does not last out here. Terry Preston has spent decades roofing homes in this exact climate, from the ranch homes near Columbia Center to the two-story houses up in the Highlands, and he builds every one for the summer it has to survive.\n\n## Our roofing & renovation services in Kennewick\n\nKennewick is home base, so we cover the full range here, roof and house alike. Whatever the job, you get a written estimate that holds and an owner who personally manages and oversees the work, not just the paperwork.\n\n- Free roof inspections with photos of your actual Kennewick roof and a plain-language walk-through, ideal after a windstorm rolls off the Columbia.\n- Roof installation built as a complete system for high-desert heat, with strong hidden materials in the valleys and eaves where a Kennewick roof fails first.\n- Roof repairs done fast, from a single lifted shingle in Southridge to failed chimney flashing on an older downtown home, with same-day and next-day service the norm.\n- Home renovation and remodeling for when the project grows past the roof, from kitchens and windows to siding and flooring, managed by the same local owner, with trusted subcontractors for specialty work.\n\n## Why Kennewick homeowners choose High Point\n\nBecause we are local, not a storm-chasing crew that blows into town after a big wind and vanishes before winter. Terry Preston is the owner, and he does your inspection and your estimate himself, then personally manages and oversees the crew on your roof. Every one of our Google reviews is five stars, and Kennewick neighbors keep naming the same three things, honesty, thoroughness, and a price that did not change. The estimate Terry writes is the price you pay, with no upselling and no mystery line items. And the good materials go into the valleys and eaves where a Kennewick roof gives out first, not just the parts you can see from the street.\n\n## Kennewick roofs: what we see and how we build for it\n\nMost Kennewick homes wear standard asphalt shingles, and in this climate the sun is what kills them. UV breaks down the shingle binder, the granules wash into the gutters, and the roof goes brittle years before its warranty says it should. The number one failure point we see is the valleys and the flashings, where afternoon heat and overnight cooling work nails loose and open small gaps that the first winter freeze pries wider. So we build for the sun and the swing, not a milder place, with synthetic felt and heavy-duty shield underneath. The best window to re-roof in Kennewick is late spring through early fall, when the weather is dry and the fresh sealant strips set fast in the heat.\n\n## Areas we serve near Kennewick\n\nKennewick is minutes from the rest of the Tri-Cities, so we roof and renovate right across the river too. We also serve nearby Pasco, Richland, and West Richland.\n\n- Pasco, Richland, West Richland",
